      "writtenOn": "2023-09-08T19:30:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As discussed OOB, it seems like you need to directly modify the stored discovery within the TCPM to get the active-cable logic to work. I think this is because you are combining multiple attempted mode entries into one test without an intervening disconnect. When you change the discovery response of the cable emulator, the TCPM will have no way of knowing that it should rerun discovery to detect that change.\n\nHypothetically, you should be able to get the TCPM to rerun discovery with a host command. A more realistic scenario would be to disconnect and reconnect the emulator inside the test.\n\nHowever, as I note below, I think that strictly from a style POV, each set of discovery responses should be its own test. Incidentally, I think this would avoid the issues you were seeing trying to get the active-cable logic to work.",
      "revId": "cabc647bf99c1cdda1d1f0236130ad67e6bcfdc5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
